  "id": "rule-governed-behavior",
  "term": "rule-governed behavior",
  "definition": "Rule-governed behavior is behavior that is analyzed as being guided by rules, and it has been used in behavior analysis to explain complex human actions such as thinking and problem-solving. In relational frame theory, it includes functional forms such as pliance and tracking.",
